        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 66-year-old male, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without pneumonic consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. He was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Clinical response was satisfactory, with improvement of respiratory function and oxygen saturation. The patient was discharged in stable condition with instructions for continuation of his inhaled therapy and a short course of oral steroids. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me with any questions.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
